# Llama Man release signing key — CURRENT (DESIGN section 12.1 step 3, section 16.2 step 3).
#
# One base64 line below: the 32 raw bytes of an ed25519 public key. It is the
# trust root for self-update, and it is compiled into the binary rather than
# fetched, because verification has to work offline with no external tooling.
#
# This is a REAL key. Its private half exists only in the `LLAMAMAN_RELEASE_KEY`
# repository secret, and `release.yml` derives the public half from that secret
# and refuses to build if it is not this value or `release-next.pub` — because a
# release signed by a key no shipped binary accepts looks, to every user, exactly
# like a corrupt download.
#
# Replacing this file is a release-engineering act. Rotation goes through
# `release-next.pub` and needs no flag day; see installer/README.md.
1PCxJhKncTAjXQVhpNENsaExLzeHTnTr/6Eystj2weY=
